doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23112942"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nealfranklin2025-cell/relay-deliberation-dataset"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/23112942"
abstract: >-
  Verbatim transcripts from a formal memory-free jury round in which four
  independent commercial AI products (Grok, Claude, ChatGPT, Perplexity) were
  consulted separately on the same research docket ("Memory as a Security
  Boundary"), with a human operator and a coordinator agent ferrying material
  between them and no direct AI-to-AI contact. Includes the coordinator's
  consolidated verdict and take/reject lists with provenance, plus two companion
  articles on the operation's open-source tool raids. The authors' claim: the
  first longitudinal dataset of human-mediated cross-model deliberation
  (unverified; see LIMITATIONS.md).
keywords:
  - multi-model deliberation
  - AI jury
  - human-in-the-loop
  - agent memory security
  - capability revocation
  - cross-model comparison
